 \section{Related Work}
 \label{sec:related}
-\paragraph{VLA policies and geometric refinement.}
-VLAs provide task-conditioned action proposals~\cite{black2024pi0,intelligence2025pi05,nvidia2025gr00t}.
-MoManipVLA transfers VLA trajectories to mobile manipulation through geometric optimization~\cite{wu2025momanipvla},
-while cuRobo and cuRoboV2 support motion generation and distance-field queries
-\cite{sundaralingam2023curobo,sundaralingam2026curobov2}. We use this policy-plus-refinement structure. Our methodological
-focus is the construction and lifetime of the contact geometry supplied to refinement, rather than a new trajectory
-optimizer or distance-field representation.
+\paragraph{Visual grounding for robot policies.}
+RoboGround learns to use grounding masks as an intermediate representation~\cite{huang2025roboground}. OBEYED-VLA separates object-centric perceptual grounding from action reasoning and uses geometry-focused observations~\cite{vo2026obeyed}. GuidedVLA specializes action-attention heads using supervision~\cite{jia2026guidedvla}. These approaches establish that task-relevant visual structure can support manipulation. Our setting instead keeps the policy frozen and extracts an observed target surface for a geometric wrapper. We do not claim that removing an external segmenter alone improves accuracy, latency, or task performance.
 
-\paragraph{Internal grounding and target extent.}
-Attention heads in frozen vision-language models can localize referred objects~\cite{kang2025fewheads}.
-KNOWS uses VLA attention to select among segmenter-produced objects and applies an ellipsoid-based safety filter
-\cite{park2026knows}. VLSA uses external visual grounding for action filtering~\cite{hu2026vlsa}, and Lan-o3dp combines
-language-guided decomposition and segmentation with collision-aware execution~\cite{li2025lano3dp}.
-\sys\ instead constructs target extent in observed depth. Its distinguishing question is how to maintain the boundary
-of a contact exception when attention is coarse, an obstacle adjoins the target, or the target becomes occluded.
-Attention selects among geometric hypotheses; it is not itself a surface-membership mask.
+\paragraph{Internal attention and feature graphs.}
+Selected attention heads can localize referred objects~\cite{kang2025fewheads}, and KNOWS already uses internal VLA attention for target selection~\cite{park2026knows}. Feature graphs are also established: TokenCut applies normalized cuts to self-supervised transformer features for object discovery~\cite{wang2022tokencut}. Our contribution is not a new graph solver or the first reuse of attention. It is a specific construction of policy-seeded observed surfaces, and a controlled investigation of whether the policy's patch descriptors should determine their boundaries. Our seed-conditioned quadratic energy differs from unsupervised spectral object discovery, but uses standard graph regularization.
 
-\paragraph{Contact-dependent collision representations.}
-MoManipVLA excludes the target mask from its real-world ESDF~\cite{wu2025momanipvla}. AutoMoMa incorporates manipulated
-objects into the robot representation during whole-body planning~\cite{niu2026automoma}; WBAG includes whole-body and
-grasp-dependent attached geometry in VLA filtering~\cite{zhen2026wbag}. Link-dependent collision permissions and attached
-objects are established planning tools. We use them to expose the consequences of visual grounding: the recovered
-target extent determines which scene surfaces can be exempted, for which configured links, and for how long. Our
-evaluation covers an audited set of relevant hand and arm links, without claiming whole-body protection.
+\paragraph{Geometric guidance and contact constraints.}
+MoManipVLA refines VLA trajectories through geometric optimization~\cite{wu2025momanipvla}; VLSA and KNOWS add safety-oriented filtering~\cite{hu2026vlsa,park2026knows}. AFI detects memory traps and intervenes using spatial affordance fields~\cite{xu2026afi}. These are related uses of geometry with different intervention mechanisms. Whole-body and attached-object constraints already appear in AutoMoMa and WBAG~\cite{niu2026automoma,zhen2026wbag}. We use link-specific permission and attachment as downstream requirements, not as independently new planning primitives. The distinguishing issue is which observed surfaces are eligible for exclusion from each collision query.
 
 \paragraph{Task state from frozen representations.}
-Sub-task prediction appears in learned VLA architectures~\cite{intelligence2025pi05,yang2025lohovla}, and probing studies
-recover progress-related information from frozen VLA features~\cite{bhardwaj2026progress,zhang2026frozenvlas}.
-Our supervised phase probe supports target-memory updates. Grasp feedback separately determines physical attachment.
-We treat the probe as a supporting component and will compare it against a strong grasp-state/history rule with the
-same geometry and controller, rather than assuming that phase classification implies reliable contact reasoning.
+Probing work recovers progress-related information from VLA representations~\cite{bhardwaj2026progress,zhang2026frozenvlas}. Our supervised sub-task probe is auxiliary. We test whether gripper state and target--hand geometry improve phase classification, and distinguish those predictions from physical confirmation of attachment. A phase label neither specifies a contact affordance nor certifies a successful grasp.
